From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:54:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 092/119] fix: the scene-referred conversion pass never
 allocated its shader reflection - the RenderThread crash on the first tick of
 the checkbox

The editor died on the RenderThread every time the Cinematic Camera's Scene
Referred checkbox was ticked: EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading address 0x4
(twice) or 0x8 (once), no resolvable module, no .dmp.

ROOT CAUSE - StandardGraphicsPipeline.cpp:107

    m_SceneReferredConvertPass.reset(new CComputeRenderPass(this));

CComputeRenderPass's flags default to eFlags_None. Without
eFlags_ReflectConstantBuffersFromShader, BeginConstantUpdate()
(ComputeRenderPass.cpp:122-136) does nothing at all - no Compile(), no
AllocateShaderReflection() - so m_pShaderReflection stays null. The
SetConstant("SceneReferredParams", ...) that follows in
ExecuteSceneReferredConversion() lands in
SDeviceObjectHelpers::CShaderConstantManager::SetNamedConstantArray
(DeviceObjectHelpers.cpp:444), whose first act after a CRY_ASSERT - compiled out
in Profile - is to read m_pShaderReflection->bValid.

SShaderReflection is { int bufferCount; bool bValid; array<SBufferUpdateContext,2>
bufferUpdateContexts; } (DeviceObjectHelpers.h:495-508): bValid sits at offset +4
and bufferUpdateContexts[0] at +8. That is the reported fault address to the byte,
and the 0x8 run is the same null pointer one member further on.

Every other compute pass in the tree that names a constant passes the flag
(TiledShading.cpp:16, VolumetricFog.cpp:157, ComputeSkinning.cpp:84, D3D_SVO.h:15).
The S3 conversion is the only one that did not, and 2026-08-28 was the first time
it ever ran.

EVIDENCE

The session log (S:\Crytek\crytek\cryengine-57-lts\5.7.1\editor.log, 10:31:15 -
NOT the project folder's editor.log, which is the accumulated crash file) shows
the flip completing and the S0/S2 reformats completing for both Sandbox graphics
pipelines before the crash:

    [SceneReferred] light-unit convention -> radiometric, 1/PI in the BRDF
    [SceneReferred] HDR satellite targets  -> R16G16B16A16F at  374x205
    [SceneReferred] scaled display targets -> R16G16B16A16F at  374x205
    [SceneReferred] HDR satellite targets  -> R16G16B16A16F at 1498x822
    [SceneReferred] scaled display targets -> R16G16B16A16F at 1498x822

There is no "HDR main targets" line because those are already fp16 at the default
r_HDRTexFormat, exactly as designed; and there is no "stock LDR post stage inert
(D9)" line, so the frame died after the reformats and before the tone map. That is
precisely where the conversion pass sits. S0's ReformatRenderTarget decision was
not the culprit; the notes are corrected to say so.

ALSO FIXED

- DeviceObjectHelpers.cpp: SetNamedConstantArray returns false on a null
  reflection instead of faulting. The same read is reachable in stock code when
  Compile() bails out on a failed resource-set update before
  AllocateShaderReflection() runs. Every other failure path in that file drops the
  constant; this one crashed.

- Texture.cpp, CTexture::ReformatRenderTarget(): two real bugs found in the audit,
  neither of them the crash.
  (a) It went straight to CreateDeviceTexture() and let SetDevTexture() drop the
      old device texture - but SetDevTexture() calls Release() on a device texture
      that FT_DONT_RELEASE has marked SetNoDelete(true), so the D3D resource was
      freed and the CDeviceTexture object leaked on every flip, per pipeline. It
      now follows CTexture::Invalidate(): ReleaseDeviceTexture(true) first, which
      raises eDeviceResourceDirty and not eResourceDestroyed, so bindings still
      rebuild and the CTexture* still never moves - the whole reason the swap
      approach was chosen over release-and-recreate is untouched.
  (b) It did not test for a target that exists as an object but has no device
      texture. Sandbox reaches that state routinely: one
      CGraphicsPipelineResources per viewport, material editor and thumbnail
      renderer. It now writes the format fields, so the target is born fp16 when
      the pool does create it, and returns without touching the device.
  It also Clear()s after the create, as SRenderTargetPool::CreateRenderTargetList()
  does. A reformat is a creation.

r_SceneReferredStage (VF_NULL, default 99)

The bisection gate. IsSceneReferred() stays the master; IsSceneReferredStage(n) is
the master ANDed with the stage, evaluated at the sites that already read the
master, so at the default it costs one integer compare and nothing moves.

  0 switch only | 1 +S0 formats | 2 +S1 exposure/AUTO | 3 +S2 units and shafts
  4 +S3 conversion | 5 +S4/S5/S7 display transform and grade | 6 +S6 export

Stage 3 is additionally enforced in
CCinematicCameraComponent::PublishSceneReferredConvention(), because Cry3DEngine's
four light-unit sites read E3DPARAM_SCENE_REFERRED and cannot see a renderer cvar.
The tone map splits its single gate into three (exposure at 2, the HDRFinalPass
SAMPLE0 permutation at 3 because the shader ties the sun-shaft composite and the
output transform to one flag, the LUTs and colour-chart skip at 5) and the
eye-adaptation mode 2 branch is now also guarded against the pinned exposure
constant. Documented in docs/ConsoleReference.md.

And one CryLogAlways at the very top of CGraphicsPipelineResources::Update(),
before any resource is touched, once per graphics pipeline per flip, so the next
crash log says how far the frame got.

CryRenderD3D11 and CinematicCamera build 0 error 0 warning. No shader changed.

