+### r_SceneReferredStage
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Default | 99 (everything) |
+| Purpose | **Bisection** switch for the scene-referred pipeline. `r_SceneReferred` is the master kill switch; this one honours the camera's request only up to a given stage, so a bad frame - or a crash - can be walked back to the one item that causes it without rebuilding anything. |
+
+Set it **before** ticking `Scene Referred` on the component, then raise it one step at a time.
+
+| Value | What is honoured |
+| --- | --- |
+| `0` | The switch and nothing else. The request is published and logged, the whole renderer stays stock. |
+| `1` | `+ S0` - the fp16 floor on the HDR render targets. Render target formats move. |
+| `2` | `+ S1` - the camera's pre-exposure and the AUTO metering. |
+| `3` | `+ S2` - the radiometric light-unit convention (1/pi in the BRDF, sun not pre-divided, sky scale) and the fp16 sun-shaft working set. |
+| `4` | `+ S3` - the Rec.709 to ACEScg working-space conversion. |
+| `5` | `+ S4 / S5 / S7` - the output transform and the camera grade: the ODT and look LUTs, the inert stock LDR stage, thresholds read as stops above mid grey. |
+| `6` | `+ S6` - the EXR export tap. |
+| `99` | Everything. Any value above 6 means the same thing. |
+
+Every gate is a plain AND with the master switch, evaluated where the master was already read, so
+at the default this cvar costs one integer compare and changes nothing.
+
+Two notes on where the boundaries actually fall. Stage 3 raises the `HDRFinalPass` permutation bit
+that selects **both** the additive sun-shaft composite (S2) and the body of the output transform
+(S4), because the shader ties them to one static flag; the LUT slots simply report a size of 0
+until stage 5, so the transform runs in its identity form in between. And stage 3 is also enforced
+inside the camera component, not only in the renderer: the four light-unit decisions that live in
+`Cry3DEngine` read `E3DPARAM_SCENE_REFERRED` and cannot see a renderer cvar, so below stage 3 the
+component simply does not publish it.
+
+When the switch flips, the renderer prints one line **per graphics pipeline** before it touches
+anything:
+
+```
+[SceneReferred] request flipped -> on, pipeline '' (stage gate r_SceneReferredStage 99, 1498x822)
+```
+
+Sandbox builds one graphics pipeline per viewport, so a normal editor flip prints this twice. It
+is the marker that says how far into the flip a frame got.
+
